## Model card

- **Identity / dates:** Exact **`gpt-5.2-pro`**,snapshot **`gpt-5.2-pro-2025-12-11`**,released **2025-12-11**,cutoff **2025-08-31**. Different from GPT-5.2 Thinking,Instant,Codex and later Pro models.[1][2]
- **Access / lifecycle:** Responses-only native model;primary page calls it previous Pro and recommends5.5Pro. Current exact OpenRouter **`openai/gpt-5.2-pro`** lists OpenAI status0,December11 backend. No exact native shutdown notice found in current deprecation log;supersession is not retirement. No authenticated inference/free Zen route verified.[1][3]
- **Context / modes:** **400,000 total/128,000 output**,medium/high/xhigh effort;some calls may take minutes,background mode recommended by primary. No base Thinking MRCR or compaction performance inherited.[1][2]
- **Modalities / tools:** **Text,image→text**,functions,file search,web search,MCP and image-generation tool documented. That tool invokes image generation;it is not evidence Pro has a native image decoder. No native audio/video claimed.[1]
- **Architecture / licence:** Proprietary closed weights;parameter counts unknown.[1]
- **Pricing (2026-10-21):** Native/current OpenAI gateway **$21 input/$168 output per1M**,no verified cached-input discount. Separate tool fees apply. ChatGPT subscription access and API token tariffs are different products;no$0 inference assumed.[1][2][3]

### Raw benchmarks found

**Attribution:** Full primary launch **Pro appendix column** and footnotes inspected. Its base Thinking column contains many results whose Pro cells are **dashes**;these are not Pro measurements. Primary defaults maximum xhigh except explicitly marked ARC high and professional-evaluation distinctions. Independent Epoch raw archive inspected for exact Pro model versions;raw versus ECI-transformed values kept separate.[2][4]

- **Professional/tool workflows:** Vendor **GDPval wins-or-ties74.1%,clear wins60.0%,no-ties67.6%**,different adjudication definitions;**investment-banking spreadsheet internal71.7%**;**BrowseComp77.9%**. These are not GDPval-AA Elo or generic tool success. Exact Tau2/Tau3,terminal,Claw-Eval/ClawProBench,MCP Atlas/Toolathlon Pro cells were not verified.[2]
- **Science/math:** Vendor **GPQA93.2% no-tools/HLE36.6% no-tools,50.0% search+Python/HMMT Feb2025 100%/AIME2025 100%**. No inference that tool-assisted HLE equals unaided reasoning or all future mathematics.[2]
- **Abstract reasoning:** Vendor **ARC-AGI1 90.5%/ARC-AGI2 54.2% high**. Epoch's externally sourced ARC records separately label **xhigh90.5%**,**high85.67%**,**medium81.17%** on ARC1,with recorded costs/task **$11.6542/$5.8694/$3.9774**;ARC2 **high54.16%/$15.721 versus medium38.47%/$8.9928**. External rows and duplicates are not multiple independent reproductions.[2][4]
- **Independent mathematics:** Epoch raw **FrontierMath Tiers1–3 v2 74.0% ±2.635percentage-point SE**,**Tier4 v2 46.0% ±7.790point SE**,exact **`gpt-5.2-pro-2025-12-11_xhigh`**,June13 runs. Earlier **Tier4 v1 webapp31.3%** is a different benchmark version/product and not combined with API v2.[4][5]
- Epoch raw **Chess Puzzles60.0% ±4.924point SE**,xhigh,October14. External SimpleBench **AVG@5 57.4%** is also reported;it is not single-attempt accuracy. Epoch ECI156.33 is on its own scale;ECI-adjusted FrontierMath77.8947% is not substituted for raw74.0%.[4]
- **Coverage gap:** Primary Pro cells for SWE-Pro,SWE Verified,SWE-Lancer,MRCR,GraphWalks,CharXiv,MMMU-Pro,VideoMMMU,ScreenSpot,Tau2 andMCP-Atlas are blank. No exact independent repair/contest/scientific coding or hard-perception score verified. A general “complex programming” description cannot numerically fill the coding axis.[2]
- Exact AA/Vals candidates404;public AA selector had no exact Pro record. BenchLM's exact profile reports no sourced coverage;Scale SWE-Pro table and additional exact Vals/LLM-Stats candidates did not supply a Pro result. These source/path findings are bounded,not a global claim that no evaluator has ever tested Pro.[6][7]

### Normalized scores (1–100)

**Not assigned.** Exact science/math/professional capability is well evidenced;absence of exact coding/perception task measurements prevents a defensible five-axis overall. No base Thinking/Codex numbers or fabricated placeholder scores used.

